R = ["At 8x8 with two interfaces the image carries the control loop's tiers (#894), SRP's Talker declarations (#895), GET_AS_PATH's read through the face (#897), AECP's REBOOT (#871), the PHY poll with its advertisement (#919, #840), the saved-state store's name marks (#920), the map edits' commit through the `EDIT` window (#923) and the StreamIDs held with their latest Talker kind (#925). In the composed flip train it plans 62.5 RAMB36: its `sram` takes a 57th granule, 752 B past 56, with 704 B of `rom` left; 62.0 before #925's StreamIDs, 672 B of `rom` past 61.5, and 61.5 before the commit. On #925's head it planned 61.0, its `sram` a 57th granule, with 816 B of `rom` left. It planned 61.0 RAMB36 on #919's head, 652 B of `rom` past 60.5, with 1,396 B left, and 60.5 on dev-soft-core `cb96336d`, 992 B of `rom` past 60.0, with 1,056 B left (680 B past at #901's merge `70f4056f`). Its entry ledgers 62.5, its measured tiles. That is the owner's rule of 2026-11-15, which supersedes the 60.5 cap of [#895's ruling of 2026-11-14](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/895#issuecomment-6876349305) (item 4, which [#897's ruling of 2026-11-15](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/897#issuecomment-6890824581), item 1, took) until S14 ([#923's ruling of 2026-11-16](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/923#issuecomment-6906679024); `ctrl_memory.LEDGERED`).\nThe owner's ruling (#665, 6505997821), and since 2026-11-12 the owner's flip decision, ledger that point, owed to lane S14, so its command adds `--interfaces 2 --ledgered-point platform-8x8-two-interfaces`.\nAt 8x8 with one interface, a shipping image, the image plans 57.5 RAMB36 in the composed train, with 232 B of `rom` left (1,136 B past 57.0 before #925's StreamIDs), and 57.0 before the commit (56.5 with the PHY poll, 1,132 B of `rom` past 56.0). Its own entry ledgers it at 57.5 by the same rule, owed to S14, so its command adds `--ledgered-point platform-8x8-one-interface`. The product SoC build (`milan_soc.add_ctrl_memory`) and this link without `--ledgered-point` plan an image at the entry whose symbols it carries (`ctrl_memory.own_point`). Every image no entry names stays refused past 56.\nEvery 1x1 point is within 56 ([split control memory](../../../../docs/design/SPLIT_CONTROL_MEMORY.md#5-fit)).\n", "- **The 8x8 images' block RAM.** At 8x8 with two interfaces the image plans 62.5 RAMB36 in the composed flip train, with the control loop's tiers (#894), SRP's Talker declarations (#895), GET_AS_PATH's read through the face (#897), the PHY poll and its advertisement (#919, #840) the map edits' commit (#923) and the StreamIDs #925 holds, its `sram` a 57th granule. That is past the 60.0 the owner's [decision of 2026-11-12](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/665#issuecomment-6824896581) ledgers for the flip and past that decision's 60.5 cap ([#895's ruling of 2026-11-14](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/895#issuecomment-6876349305), item 4). Its entry is 62.5, refused at 63.0, by the owner's rule of 2026-11-15 ([#923's ruling of 2026-11-16](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/923#issuecomment-6906679024)): debt of 6.5 RAMB36 owed to lane S14 (decision D3), 26,624 B of cold code to move to flash. At 8x8 with one interface it plans 57.5, its own entry by the same rule, refused at 58.0: ROM debt of 1.5 RAMB36, 6,144 B, owed to S14. [`plat_ledger.py`](../../../../tb/verilator/ctrl_split_boot/plat_ledger.py) links the image at every point against the ledger ([SPLIT_CONTROL_MEMORY.md section 5](../../../../docs/design/SPLIT_CONTROL_MEMORY.md#5-fit)).\n"]
